[1.1857151679978415, "o", "SENSAI | PROFILES\nActual component execution; fictional Atelier Nova data."]
[1.1857390529985423, "o", "\n"]
[1.9866211919979833, "o", "\n\u001b[36m>>> /prefs add: Camille prefers concise English test summaries\u001b[0m"]
[1.9866475929993612, "o", "\n"]
[2.003630464998423, "o", "Preferences updated successfully.\n"]
[2.804625117998512, "o", "\n\u001b[36m>>> /inst add: preserve the payment module\u001b[0m"]
[2.804647117998684, "o", "\n"]
[2.8157297789985023, "o", "Instructions updated successfully.\n"]
[3.6167615889971785, "o", "\n\u001b[36m>>> build_messages: inspect the profile context injected into a turn\u001b[0m"]
[3.616781632998027, "o", "\n"]
[3.616889747998357, "o", "{\n  \"role\": \"system\",\n  \"content\": \"User preferences: Use concise English summaries and pytest -q.\\nInstructions (YOU MUST FOLLOW): Do not edit payment code.\"\n}"]
[3.616915519000031, "o", "\n"]
[4.424486658997921, "o", "\n\u001b[36m>>> Camille > Which test command should I use and which module must I leave untouched? Answer using my saved preferences and instructions, not an assumed convention.\u001b[0m"]
[4.424499090997415, "o", "\n"]
[5.103966716000286, "o", "Based on your saved preferences and instructions, you should use the pytest -q  \ncommand, and the module that must remain untouched is the payment code.         \n"]
[5.120233783000003, "o", "\n"]
[5.120247961000132, "o", "\n"]
[5.924062394999055, "o", "\n\u001b[36m>>> Log out, then authenticate the same fictional profile\u001b[0m"]
[5.924078738000389, "o", "\n"]
[6.054048627000157, "o", "{\n  \"profile\": \"Camille\",\n  \"preferences\": \"Use concise English summaries and pytest -q.\",\n  \"instructions\": \"Do not edit payment code.\"\n}"]
[6.054063084000518, "o", "\n"]
[6.855088257998432, "o", "\n\u001b[36m>>> A wrong demo password does not authenticate\u001b[0m"]
[6.855113680998329, "o", "\n"]
[6.982376791998831, "o", "{\n  \"authenticated\": false\n}"]
[6.982388873999298, "o", "\n"]
[7.983522276997974, "o", "\nComponent demonstration completed."]
[7.983537083997362, "o", "\n"]
